<article class="env-example" id="F391B4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F391B4">Example <span data-tag="F391B4">5.2.8.16</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos and let $n \geq -2$ be an integer. Then there exists a factorization system $(S_ L, S_ R)$ on $\calX $, where $S_ L$ denotes the collection of $(n+1)$-connective morphisms of $\calX $ and $S_ R$ the collection of $n$-truncated morphisms of $\calC $. See §<a href="/tag/548553" data-tag="548553">6.5.1</a>. </p>
